+/*
+ * Ticks must not merge in the PIC. When the timer runs late, the transitions it
+ * missed are replayed back to back; a rising edge that reaches the PIC while the
+ * previous tick is still waiting there (IRR set, not yet taken by the CPU) is lost,
+ * and a guest that counts ticks to keep time (Windows 9x: timeGetTime, and games
+ * timed by it) slows down. On a Windows host, where timers fire late, a 1 kHz tick
+ * lost about a third of its ticks. So hold such an edge back briefly and retry,
+ * unless the guest masked the line; a backlog of more than PIT_MAX_BACKLOG ticks
+ * (after the VM was paused, say) is dropped rather than fast-forwarded.
+ */
+#define PIT_RETRY_NS     20000
+#define PIT_MAX_BACKLOG  100
+
